.TH "DISABLE-TOUCHPAD.SH" "1" "November 2026" "arran4/dotfiles" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
disable\-touchpad.sh \- disable a touchpad with xinput
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBdisable\-touchpad.sh\fR
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Find an XInput device whose name contains TouchPad and set its Device Enabled property to 0. This is an X11/XInput helper, not a Wayland touchpad configuration method.
.SH NOTES
The device match is name\-based. Review xinput list before using on an unfamiliar X11 machine.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Requires X11, xinput, grep and sed. The script searches for
a device name containing the exact case-sensitive text TouchPad.
It does not work as a touchpad-management interface in a native
Wayland session.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
xinput list --short
disable-touchpad.sh
xinput list-props DEVICE_ID
xinput enable DEVICE_ID
.fi
.PP
Replace DEVICE_ID with a device number obtained from xinput.
The final command re-enables a disabled device using xinput.
.SH LIMITATIONS
More than one matching touchpad, no matching touchpad or an unusual
device name may cause incorrect selection or failure. The helper
does not remember or restore the previous device state. On
Hyprland/Wayland, configure the actual input device instead.
